UID:d99f3bb9c3187444@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T220717Z
SEQUENCE:2026091422
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 6:00 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 5:45 PM.\nOn stage: 7:00 PM–7:45 PM.\nACT I 
 Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — pr
 oduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time danc
 ers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Tim
 e.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiv
 ing and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are cal
 led unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedul
 e\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mast
 er: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N
 7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Rats ***\nRats — C
 ostume (you provide): Male: Black tights\, black fitted t-shirt Female: 
 Black Seamless Tights\, Black or Flesh tone Camisole Leotard\; Shoes: Bl
 ack Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Male: Hair out of 
 the eyes Female: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): Gloves\
 nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Powder matching skintone\n
 • Light brown eye shadow applied to the crease with an eye shadow brus
 h\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n•
  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look w
 ashed out in the stage lights)\n• Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of
  Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume 
 Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with care while changing to 
 prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas 
 in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how
  significant\n• Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or 
 hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the f
 loor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or l
 aunder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in 
 costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on co
 stume during its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume or c
 ologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garment not assigned to cast
  member\n• Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\
 , with the exception of water\n• Do not remove costumes from their ass
 igned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used
  to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n• Return all head
 pieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates
  to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, pain
 ts\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
